# Miscellaneous
*.class
*.log
*.lock
# ...except the app's. The blanket rule above comes from Dart's template for
# LIBRARIES, where a lock file would over-constrain consumers. This repo ships
# an application, and CI without a lock resolves its own dependency set on
# every run: on 7 Sep 2026 that picked sqlite3 3.5.2, whose prebuilt
# libsqlite3.x64.linux.so failed its own hash check, and the AAB build died in
# a package no commit had touched. The lock is how CI builds what was tested.
!flutter_vocabmaster/pubspec.lock
*.pyc
*.swp
.DS_Store
.atom/
.buildlog/
.history
.svn/

